# UI

Read `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` before touching anything here.

## Transcribe, do not translate

The design is 560 lines where every value is an inline `style` attribute. We
**transcribe them verbatim**. No Tailwind, no CSS modules, no component
abstraction over the design's own markup. It is repetitive on purpose: a shared
utility would read better and would let the rendered result drift from the
approved design without the diff showing it.

`app/globals.css` is the design's own `<helmet>` stylesheet and nothing else.

## The two colour layers disagree ON PURPOSE

Six values differ between the `[data-theme]` blocks and the `renderVals()`
literals (`--ink2`, `--rule`, `--on`, `--grnbg`, `--goldbg`, `--badbg`).
**Both are correct.** The helmet wins where markup resolves `var(--x, …)`; the
`PROP` layer in `lib/design.ts` wins where the value arrives as a prop.

**Reconciling them is the bug, not the fix.** `corepack pnpm lint` fails if you
do. So does `tests/unit/design-contract.test.ts`.

Inline fallbacks like `var(--ink3, rgba(166,201,180,0.58))` are dead code in the
live DOM. Transcribe them verbatim anyway. Never "correct" them.

## Fonts

Anton (titles/numbers, 400 only) · Oswald (all UI caps, always tracked) ·
Archivo (body) · JetBrains Mono (meta, tokens, serials, plates).

Loaded via `@fontsource`, **not `next/font`** — next/font generates obfuscated
family names and the design names families as literals, so every one would
silently fall back to a system face. Every declared weight must be imported;
`scripts/audit-font-weights.mjs` proves it.

Anton headings render **synthesised bold** — the design does this too (verified:
`font-weight: 700`, `font-synthesis: auto`, only Anton 400 loaded). Do not add
`font-synthesis: none`.

## Definition of done for any UI change

```
corepack pnpm lint && corepack pnpm test:visual
```

`test:visual` compares against `design/reference/`, captured from the approved
bundle rendering itself. ≤0.8%. Both themes, both viewports. If it fails, open
the `.diff.png` in `test-results/visual/` — do not regenerate the reference to
make it pass.

Responsive: the design's Web/Mob toggle is a review affordance and is **not**
shipped. `mob ? A : B` becomes a media query at 768px.
